preConditionHook:
// A failed breakout of the opening gap. The session gapped BELOW the prior
// session's low, the session's FIRST bar closed as a bull reversal bar, and
// the second bar of the session now closes back above that first bar's high
// -- buy. Short is the mirror after a gap above the prior session's high.
//
// The gate is barsIn == 2: the bar being judged is the session's SECOND bar,
// so bar [1] is the session's first bar. barsIn is the standing
// bars-into-session counter, 1 on the first bar of the session, reset at the
// wall-clock close-date change day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)) per
// the session model decision. Written through the counter rather than as a
// date comparison at an offset so that the same statement serves both twins
// and matches the rest of the session family.
//
// prevHigh / prevLow ARE HighD(1) / LowD(1), which the twin calls and the
// engine does not expose. MEASURED (the highd/lowd register row): the day is
// the wall-clock CALENDAR date, the SAME boundary as date <> date[1]; xxxD(0)
// is the running value INCLUSIVE of the current bar; the prior-day forms
// return a -1 SENTINEL while fewer than that many complete days exist. Read
// on the session's second bar they still refer to the day before this one.
//
// WARM-UP, as in FailedBreakoutOfPriorSessionExtreme: TradeStation's HighD
// reads the chart's own data and answers on the first evaluated bar, while
// this mirror sees only bars from Max Bars Back on. sawStart makes that
// honest -- a day becomes 'the prior session' only once its own first bar has
// been observed -- so the mirror is silent through the first partial day and
// the first fully observed day and the twins agree exactly from the second
// date change on.
//
// KEPT WHOLE, and it is not SessionBarBreakout with filters bolted on: every
// added term reads bar [1], the session's FIRST bar, from the vantage of bar
// [0], and no placement in the corpus can state 'the session's first bar
// gapped below yesterday's low and closed as a bull reversal bar' at that
// offset. Kept apart from FailedBreakoutOfPriorSessionExtreme (any bar of the
// session, no gap and no reversal-bar term) and from GapPullbackFailureEntry
// (an intraday retracement into the gap instead). Intraday bars only.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    if (sawStart) {
        prevHigh = curHigh;
        prevLow = curLow;
    }
    sawStart = true;
    curHigh = high[0];
    curLow = low[0];
    barsIn = 1;
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
    if (el_gt(high[0], curHigh)) curHigh = high[0];
    if (el_lt(low[0], curLow)) curLow = low[0];
}
firstBull = el_gt(close[1], open[1])
    && el_ge(close[1] - open[1], bodyFraction * (high[1] - low[1]));
firstBear = el_lt(close[1], open[1])
    && el_ge(open[1] - close[1], bodyFraction * (high[1] - low[1]));
longSig = (barsIn == 2) && !el_eq(prevLow, -1.0) && el_lt(open[1], prevLow)
    && firstBull && el_gt(close[0], high[1]);
shortSig = (barsIn == 2) && !el_eq(prevHigh, -1.0) && el_gt(open[1], prevHigh)
    && firstBear && el_lt(close[0], low[1]);
